# Architecture

This document describes the current implemented structure, ownership, dependency direction, process boundaries, storage, and external boundaries. Update it when architecture changes; put long-lived alternatives and rationale in `docs/design-docs/` or `docs/decisions/`.

## Current system map

{{ARCHITECTURE_EVIDENCE}}

The durable target follows a host/project-owned path:

```text
host/project workflow
    -> AGENTS.md
    -> docs/README.md
    -> one matching active Markdown Plan
    -> task-relevant current authority
    -> project-owned commands and evidence
```

The generated target is independent after setup. Its documents, Plans, runbooks, Git history, project commands, and host-native Agents remain useful when the setup package is absent. No package runtime, command wrapper, task store, or hidden execution state is part of this target.

## Durable generated structure

```text
AGENTS.md                         canonical host-neutral entry point
CLAUDE.md                         optional exact host adapter: @AGENTS.md
ARCHITECTURE.md                   current structure and dependency direction

docs/
  README.md                       knowledge and generated-surface map
  PRODUCT.md                      current product boundary
  DESIGN.md                       current design principles
  QUALITY.md                      project-owned checks and evidence policy
  OPERATIONS.md                   current operational authority
  SECURITY.md                     security boundary and reporting
  PLANS.md                        compact Plan lifecycle
  product-specs/                  versioned requirements
  design-docs/                    durable designs
  decisions/                     decision history
  exec-plans/
    _template.md                 compact `format: 2` Plan contract
    active/                      current substantive work
    completed/                   terminal historical outcomes
    tech-debt-tracker.md         bounded out-of-scope discoveries
  references/                    durable protocols and explanatory notes
  runbooks/
    index.md                     static runbook catalog
    _template.md                 manual runbook template
    <slug>.md                    ordinary Markdown for eligible procedures
```

Only complete, unique, user-confirmed strict nine-field procedure records qualify for static runbooks. The exact fields are `slug`, `title`, `trigger`, `reads`, `actions`, `stop_conditions`, `evidence`, `permissions`, and `rollback`. The rendered `docs/runbooks/<slug>.md` is ordinary Markdown with no frontmatter, executor metadata, hooks, command registration, or privilege-bearing configuration. Incomplete, malformed, generic, inferred, Proposed, Open, Sources-only, or duplicate records produce no runbook.

## Ownership and dependency direction

### Confirmed

- Canonical authority is routed from `AGENTS.md` through `docs/README.md` to the task-relevant current document and one matching Plan.
- Project commands, tests, CI, deployment, operations, secrets, Git, and acceptance evidence are project-owned.
- The optional host adapter points only to `AGENTS.md`; canonical documents do not depend on that adapter.
- Plans refer to project-owned commands, and generated documents do not import package code.

### Proposed

- None.

### Open

- Identify module owners, stable interfaces, dependency direction, and where boundaries are enforced for this project.

